-- Social Security Benefits Up-rating Order 2026 (S.I. 2026/148) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
-- (A plain-text rendering of the version on legislation.gov.uk dated 2026-03-05, not the official text.)
--
-- SEAT: the person who receives, or may claim, a benefit or payment the Order up-rates, and who asks what the weekly
-- rate or amount is for them, from when, and where the Order applies to them.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the modules imported above as the questions that person asks. Nothing
-- here is new law. Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list), one for each
-- fact the person states, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. Where a module's rule wants a record
-- (the two members of a couple in Schedule 8 (3)), the record is built inside the question, in its WHERE, from those
-- answers and the same module rule is called; no rule is restated here. The only code here besides calls is thin
-- selection: reading the figure after the Order out of a sum and its replacement, and choosing among the six identical
-- non-dependant deduction tables.
--
-- WHAT THE ORDER DOES. It states, for the 2026-27 year, the new weekly figures for a long list of benefits. The figures
-- stand in other instruments (the Contributions and Benefits Act 1992, the Income Support Regulations and so on), which
-- are not among the inputs. So most questions are lookups ("what is the sum in this place after the Order?") and a few are
-- the Order's own percentage increases, where the person gives the sum they have now.
--
-- NOT COVERED. A question asked about a row the text does not print, or about a person no printed row reaches, is answered
-- NOTHING, never a guess. Where the Order amends a sum only 'as it has effect in' a stated kind of case, a person outside
-- that kind of case is answered NOTHING.
--
-- Where this layer departs from the defaults ruled on 2026-10-18 (recorded, not fixed):
--   * The Order is an amending instrument; the parent instruments' own rules are not encoded. A question the Order cannot
--     answer by itself (whether a person satisfies the condition in a paragraph of a parent instrument) is asked as a fact.
--   * One case is one claim for one benefit; a person who claims several benefits asks the questions of each.

-- Dates in the Order run from fixed days and, for most benefits, from the first day of the claimant's first benefit week
-- or assessment period on or after 6 April 2026. What a benefit week or an assessment period is lies in other
-- instruments, so the dates are asked.
§ `The Order: where and when it applies to me, and what its short names mean (articles 1 and 2)`

-- art 1(2): articles 14 and 15 and parts of articles 3 and 7 extend to England and Wales only; everything else extends
-- to both.
@export Does this provision of the Order extend to where I live (art 1(2))?
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `a provision whose extent art 1(2) states` @desc Which provision of the Order is it?
      `where I live` IS A `a territory` @desc Where do you live?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this provision of the Order extend to where I live` IF
    `art 1(2): the provision extends to the territory` `the provision` `where I live`

-- art 1(3): each group of articles has its own date; art 1(4): for unearned income under a universal credit award,
-- articles 3, 4, 5, 6, 9, 11, 12, 13, 16, 17, 18, 28 and 31 take effect on the first day of the first assessment period
-- instead.
@export On what date does this article of the Order come into force for me (art 1(3) and (4))?
GIVEN `the article` IS A NUMBER @desc Which article of the Order is it (a number from 1 to 34)?
      `it is an increase to which article 7(9)(b) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an increase to which article 7(9)(b) applies (the earnings limit for an adult dependant)?
      `it is for the rate of my maternity allowance under section 35A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for determining the rate of your maternity allowance under section 35A(1)?
      `my rent is payable weekly or at a multiple of a week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your rent payable weekly, or at a multiple of a week?
      `the first day of my first benefit week on or after 6 April 2026` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of your first benefit week that begins on or after 6 April 2026?
      `I have a universal credit award in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a universal credit award in force?
      `it is for my unearned income under that award` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question about your unearned income under that universal credit award?
      `the first day of my first assessment period on or after 6 April 2026` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of your first universal credit assessment period that begins on or after 6 April 2026?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what date does this article of the Order come into force for me` IS
    `art 1(3) and (4): the date on which the article comes into force for the beneficiary` `the article` `it is an increase to which article 7(9)(b) applies` `it is for the rate of my maternity allowance under section 35A(1)` `my rent is payable weekly or at a multiple of a week` `the first day of my first benefit week on or after 6 April 2026` `I have a universal credit award in force` `it is for my unearned income under that award` `the first day of my first assessment period on or after 6 April 2026`

-- art 1(5): the changes made by articles 3, 4, 5, 6, 11, 12 and 13, and article 25(b) so far as it concerns an adult
-- dependant's earnings, take effect on the date article 7 gives for the case.
@export Does the change in my sum take effect on the date article 7 specifies (art 1(5))?
GIVEN `the article` IS A NUMBER @desc Which article of the Order is it (a number from 1 to 34)?
      `the sum is the article 25(b) earnings limit for an adult dependant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sum the article 25(b) earnings limit for an adult dependant?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the change in my sum take effect on the date article 7 specifies` IF
    `art 1(5): the change in the sums takes effect on the date article 7 specifies` `the article` `the sum is the article 25(b) earnings limit for an adult dependant`

-- art 2: fourteen short names.
@export What does this short name in the Order stand for (art 2)?
GIVEN `the short name` IS A `a short name defined by art 2` @desc Which short name does the Order use?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `What does this short name in the Order stand for` IS
    `art 2: the instrument that the short name means` `the short name`

§ `Part 2: pensions, benefits and statutory payments (articles 3 to 19 and Schedule 1)`

§§ `Schedule 4 to the Contributions and Benefits Act (article 3)`

-- art 3: the sums in Parts I, III, IV and V of Schedule 4 are those of Schedule 1 to the Order, except age addition and
-- guardian's allowance in Part III and the child increases in Part V.
@export What does article 3 do to this sum in Schedule 4 to the Contributions and Benefits Act (art 3)?
GIVEN `the sum` IS A `a sum in Schedule 4 to the Contributions and Benefits Act` @desc Which sum in Schedule 4 to the Contributions and Benefits Act is it?
GIVETH A `what art 3 does to a sum in Schedule 4`
DECIDE `What does article 3 do to this sum in Schedule 4 to the Contributions and Benefits Act` IS
    `art 3: what the article does to the sum` `the sum`

§§ `Retirement pension and related sums (articles 4 to 6)`

@export What is my retirement allowance sum after the increase of 3.8 per cent (art 4(1))?
GIVEN `my sum under paragraph 13(4) of Schedule 7 before the Order` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the sum calculated under paragraph 13(4) of Schedule 7 to the Contributions and Benefits Act now, before the Order, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my retirement allowance sum after the increase of 3.8 per cent` IS
    `art 4(1): the retirement allowance sum after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `my sum under paragraph 13(4) of Schedule 7 before the Order`

@export What is the sum in section 44(4) of the Contributions and Benefits Act after the Order (art 4(2))?
GIVEN `the sum in section 44(4)` IS A `a sum in section 44(4) of the Contributions and Benefits Act that art 4(2) replaces` @desc Which sum in section 44(4) is it?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the sum in section 44(4) of the Contributions and Benefits Act after the Order` IS
    (`art 4(2): the replaced and the replacing sum` `the sum in section 44(4)`)'s `the sum after the Order`

-- art 4(3)(a): an additional pension is increased only where the final relevant year is earlier than the tax year
-- 2025-26.
@export What is my pension sum after the increase of 3.8 per cent (art 4(3))?
GIVEN `the kind of sum` IS A `a sum that art 4(3) directs to be increased` @desc Which kind of sum is it?
      `the first calendar year of my final relevant year` IS A NUMBER @desc For an additional pension: what is the first calendar year of the final relevant year (for the tax year 2024-25, give 2024)? Otherwise give 0.
      `my sum before the increase` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the sum now, before the Order, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my pension sum after the increase of 3.8 per cent` IS
    `art 4(3): the sum after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `the kind of sum` `the first calendar year of my final relevant year` `my sum before the increase`

@export What is my shared additional pension after the increase of 3.8 per cent (art 4(4)(a))?
GIVEN `my shared additional pension before the Order` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your shared additional pension under section 55A or 55AA now, before the Order, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my shared additional pension after the increase of 3.8 per cent` IS
    `art 4(4)(a): the shared additional pension after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `my shared additional pension before the Order`

@export What is my increase under paragraph 2 of Schedule 5A after the increase of 3.8 per cent (art 4(4)(b))?
GIVEN `my increase under paragraph 2 of Schedule 5A before the Order` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the increase in your shared additional pension under paragraph 2 of Schedule 5A now, before the Order, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my increase under paragraph 2 of Schedule 5A after the increase of 3.8 per cent` IS
    `art 4(4)(b): the paragraph 2 of Schedule 5A increase after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `my increase under paragraph 2 of Schedule 5A before the Order`

-- art 5: increased by 3.8 per cent for earnings factors of 1987-88 and earlier, by 0.8 per cent for 1988-89 to 1996-97;
-- the Order says nothing about later years.
@export What is my guaranteed minimum increase after the Order (art 5)?
GIVEN `the first calendar year of the tax year of my earnings factors` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first calendar year of the tax year of the earnings factors the increase is attributable to (for 1987-88, give 1987)?
      `my sum under section 15(1) of the Pension Schemes Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the sum payable under section 15(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 1993 now, before the Order, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my guaranteed minimum increase after the Order` IS
    `art 5: the guaranteed minimum increase after the increase` `the first calendar year of the tax year of my earnings factors` `my sum under section 15(1) of the Pension Schemes Act`

@export What is the full rate of the state pension after the Order (art 6(1))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the full rate of the state pension after the Order` IS
    (`art 6(1): regulation 1A of the State Pension Regulations 2015, the full rate of state pension`)'s `the sum after the Order`

@export What is my section 17 increase to the state pension after the increase of 3.8 per cent (art 6(2))?
GIVEN `my increase under section 17 before the Order` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the increase under section 17 of the Pensions Act 2014 in the rate of your state pension now, before the Order, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my section 17 increase to the state pension after the increase of 3.8 per cent` IS
    `art 6(2): the section 17 increase after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `my increase under section 17 before the Order`

@export What is my state pension amount after the increase of 3.8 per cent (art 6(3))?
GIVEN `the kind of amount` IS A `an amount that art 6(3) increases` @desc Which kind of amount is it?
      `my amount before the increase` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount now, before the Order, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my state pension amount after the increase of 3.8 per cent` IS
    `art 6(3): the amount after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `the kind of amount` `my amount before the increase`

-- Article 1 says when each article comes into force; article 7 says from when the changes in the sums of articles 3, 4,
-- 5, 6, 11, 12 and 13 take effect for each case.
§§ `Dates on which the changes take effect (article 7)`

-- art 7: each change takes effect on its own date; carer's allowance paid on a Wednesday takes the increase two days
-- later; the article 25(b) earnings limit takes effect from the first benefit week to begin on or after 6 April 2026 (1
-- April if regulation 7(b) applies).
@export On what date does the change in my benefit take effect (art 7)?
GIVEN `the change` IS A `a change that art 7 dates` @desc Which change is it?
      `my carer's allowance is paid on a Wednesday` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State arranged for your carer's allowance to be paid on a Wednesday?
      `regulation 7(b) of the Computation of Earnings Regulations applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 7(b) of the Social Security Benefit (Computation of Earnings) Regulations 1996 apply to you?
      `the first day of my first benefit week for the earnings limit` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of your first benefit week that begins on or after 1 April 2026 (if regulation 7(b) applies) or 6 April 2026 (if not)?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what date does the change in my benefit take effect` IS
    `art 7: the date on which the change takes effect` `the change` `my carer's allowance is paid on a Wednesday` `regulation 7(b) of the Computation of Earnings Regulations applies to me` `the first day of my first benefit week for the earnings limit`

§§ `Statutory payments (articles 8 to 10)`

@export What is the weekly rate of my statutory payment after the Order (arts 8 to 10)?
GIVEN `the kind of statutory pay` IS A `a kind of statutory pay whose weekly rate arts 8 to 10 state` @desc Which statutory payment is it?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the weekly rate of my statutory payment after the Order` IS
    (`arts 8 to 10: the replaced and the replacing weekly rate` `the kind of statutory pay`)'s `the sum after the Order`

§§ `Graduated retirement benefit and Category C and maximum additional pensions (articles 11 to 13)`

-- art 11(1): stated in pence: 17.83 pence increased by 3.8 per cent is stated as 18.51 pence. The exact product is
-- 18.50754 (see NOTES.md).
@export What is the sum of graduated retirement benefit in pence after the Order (art 11(1))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the sum of graduated retirement benefit in pence after the Order` IS
    (`art 11(1): section 36(1) of the National Insurance Act 1965, the sum of graduated retirement benefit, in pence`)'s `the sum after the Order`

@export What is my graduated retirement sum after the increase of 3.8 per cent (art 11(2) to (4))?
GIVEN `the kind of sum` IS A `a sum that art 11 increases by 3.8 per cent` @desc Which kind of sum is it?
      `my sum before the increase` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the sum now, before the Order, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my graduated retirement sum after the increase of 3.8 per cent` IS
    `art 11(2) to (4): the sum after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `the kind of sum` `my sum before the increase`

@export What is the Category C retirement pension for widows after the Order (art 12)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the Category C retirement pension for widows after the Order` IS
    (`art 12: regulation 11(3) of the Social Security (Widow's Benefit and Retirement Pensions) Regulations 1979, the Category C retirement pension for widows of men over pensionable age on 5th July 1948`)'s `the sum after the Order`

@export What is the maximum additional pension for survivors after the Order (art 13)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the maximum additional pension for survivors after the Order` IS
    (`art 13: regulation 3A of the Social Security (Maximum Additional Pension) Regulations 2010, the prescribed maximum additional pension for survivors who become entitled on or after 6th April 2016`)'s `the sum after the Order`

§§ `Disability and incapacity benefits (articles 14 to 17)`

@export What is my weekly rate of disability living allowance after the Order (art 14)?
GIVEN `the paragraph of regulation 4` IS A `a paragraph of regulation 4 of the Disability Living Allowance Regulations 1991` @desc Which paragraph of regulation 4 of the Disability Living Allowance Regulations 1991 gives your rate?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my weekly rate of disability living allowance after the Order` IS
    (`art 14: the replaced and the replacing weekly rate` `the paragraph of regulation 4`)'s `the sum after the Order`

@export What is my weekly rate of personal independence payment after the Order (art 15)?
GIVEN `the paragraph of regulation 24` IS A `a paragraph of regulation 24 of the Personal Independence Payment Regulations 2013` @desc Which paragraph of regulation 24 of the Personal Independence Payment Regulations 2013 gives your rate?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my weekly rate of personal independence payment after the Order` IS
    (`art 15: the replaced and the replacing weekly rate` `the paragraph of regulation 24`)'s `the sum after the Order`

-- art 16(2): a claimant entitled to long-term incapacity benefit who was subject to regulation 2(3) of the 2008
-- Regulations has the sums increased to 15.50 and 8.60; art 16(1) is subject to that.
@export What is my age addition to incapacity benefit after the Order (art 16)?
GIVEN `the sub-paragraph of regulation 10(2)` IS A `a sub-paragraph of regulation 10(2) of the Incapacity Benefit Regulations 1994` @desc Which sub-paragraph of regulation 10(2) of the Incapacity Benefit Regulations 1994 gives your rate?
      `I am entitled to long-term incapacity benefit and was subject to regulation 2(3) of the 2008 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to long-term incapacity benefit and were you subject to regulation 2(3) of the Employment and Support Allowance (Up-rating Modification) (Transitional) Regulations 2008?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my age addition to incapacity benefit after the Order` IS
    `art 16: the sum in regulation 10(2) after the Order` `the sub-paragraph of regulation 10(2)` `I am entitled to long-term incapacity benefit and was subject to regulation 2(3) of the 2008 Regulations`

@export What is my transitional invalidity allowance sum after the Order (art 17)?
GIVEN `the sub-paragraph of regulation 18(2)` IS A `a sub-paragraph of regulation 18(2) of the Incapacity Benefit (Transitional) Regulations 1995` @desc Which sub-paragraph of regulation 18(2) of the Incapacity Benefit (Transitional) Regulations 1995 gives your rate?
      `I am entitled to long-term incapacity benefit and was subject to regulation 2(3) of the 2008 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to long-term incapacity benefit and were you subject to regulation 2(3) of the Employment and Support Allowance (Up-rating Modification) (Transitional) Regulations 2008?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my transitional invalidity allowance sum after the Order` IS
    `art 17: the sum in regulation 18(2) after the Order` `the sub-paragraph of regulation 18(2)` `I am entitled to long-term incapacity benefit and was subject to regulation 2(3) of the 2008 Regulations`

§§ `Bereavement benefits (articles 18 and 19)`

@export What is my weekly rate of bereavement benefit after the Order (art 18)?
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A `a regulation of the Rate of Bereavement Benefits Regulations 2010` @desc Which benefit is it?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my weekly rate of bereavement benefit after the Order` IS
    (`art 18: the replaced and the replacing weekly rate` `the benefit`)'s `the sum after the Order`

-- art 19: all four sums remain unchanged.
@export What is my bereavement support payment sum after the Order (art 19)?
GIVEN `the paragraph of regulation 3` IS A `a paragraph of regulation 3 of the Bereavement Support Payment Regulations 2017` @desc Which paragraph of regulation 3 of the Bereavement Support Payment Regulations 2017 gives your sum?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my bereavement support payment sum after the Order` IS
    (`art 19: the sum, replaced or restated as unchanged` `the paragraph of regulation 3`)'s `the sum after the Order`

§§ `Schedule 1: the weekly rates in Schedule 4 to the Contributions and Benefits Act`

@export What is my weekly rate of a contributory benefit in Part I of Schedule 4 (Sch 1 Part I)?
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A `a weekly rate in Part I of Schedule 4` @desc Which benefit is it?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my weekly rate of a contributory benefit in Part I of Schedule 4` IS
    `Sch 1 Part I: the weekly rate` `the benefit`

-- Part III item 8 prints 0.25 for age addition although article 3(2)(a) excepts it from the increase; the Schedule
-- states the figure (see NOTES.md).
@export What is my weekly rate of a non-contributory benefit in Part III of Schedule 4 (Sch 1 Part III)?
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A `a weekly rate in Part III of Schedule 4` @desc Which benefit is it?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my weekly rate of a non-contributory benefit in Part III of Schedule 4` IS
    `Sch 1 Part III: the weekly rate` `the benefit`

-- Part IV item 1A speaks of a beneficiary 'under' or 'over' pensionable age; a beneficiary exactly at pensionable age is
-- in neither, and the answer is NOTHING (see NOTES.md).
@export What is my increase for an adult dependant after the Order (Sch 1 Part IV)?
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A `a benefit with an increase for an adult dependant in Part IV` @desc Which benefit do you get the increase with?
      `my position relative to pensionable age` IS A `a position relative to pensionable age` @desc Are you under, at, or over pensionable age?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my increase for an adult dependant after the Order` IS
    `Sch 1 Part IV: the increase for an adult dependant` `the benefit` `my position relative to pensionable age`

-- Part V item 1: the table prints degrees from 100 to 20 in steps of 10; any other degree is not in the text.
@export What is my weekly disablement pension for my degree of disablement (Sch 1 Part V item 1)?
GIVEN `my degree of disablement in per cent` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your degree of disablement, in per cent (20, 30, ... 100)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my weekly disablement pension for my degree of disablement` IS
    `Sch 1 Part V item 1: the weekly rate of disablement pension for the degree of disablement` `my degree of disablement in per cent`

@export What is the most I can be paid for constant attendance with my disablement pension (Sch 1 Part V item 2)?
GIVEN `my disablement is exceptionally severe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your disablement exceptionally severe?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be paid for constant attendance with my disablement pension` IS
    `Sch 1 Part V item 2: the maximum increase of the weekly rate of disablement pension where constant attendance is needed` `my disablement is exceptionally severe`

@export What is my increase of unemployability supplement (Sch 1 Part V item 6)?
GIVEN `my age on the qualifying date` IS A NUMBER @desc How old were you on the qualifying date?
      `the qualifying date fell before 5 July 1948` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the qualifying date fall before 5 July 1948?
      `I had attained pensionable age before 6 April 1979` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had you attained pensionable age before 6 April 1979?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my increase of unemployability supplement` IS
    `Sch 1 Part V item 6: the increase of the weekly rate of unemployability supplement` `my age on the qualifying date` `the qualifying date fell before 5 July 1948` `I had attained pensionable age before 6 April 1979`

-- Part V item 10(c): 30 per cent of the first sum specified in section 44(4). The Order does not say which of its two
-- section 44(4) sums that is, so it is asked.
@export What is my widow's pension at the lower permanent rate (Sch 1 Part V item 10(c))?
GIVEN `the first sum specified in section 44(4) of the Contributions and Benefits Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first sum specified in section 44(4) of the Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (the Category A basic retirement pension), in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my widow's pension at the lower permanent rate` IS
    `Sch 1 Part V item 10(c): the widow's pension at the lower permanent rate` `the first sum specified in section 44(4) of the Contributions and Benefits Act`

@export What is my single-figure industrial injuries rate (Sch 1 Part V)?
GIVEN `the row` IS A `a single-figure row of Part V of Schedule 4` @desc Which row of Part V of Schedule 4 do you ask about?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my single-figure industrial injuries rate` IS
    `Sch 1 Part V: the single figure` `the row`

§ `Part 3: income support and housing benefit (articles 20 to 24 and Schedules 2 to 7)`

§§ `Income support: sums (articles 20 to 22)`

-- art 20(2): the sum specified in each of five places is 3,000 and remains unchanged.
@export What is the sum of 3,000 in the income support rules after the Order (art 20(2))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the sum of 3,000 in the income support rules after the Order` IS
    (`art 20(2): regulations 17(1)(b), 18(1)(c) and 21(1) and paragraphs 13A(2)(a) and 14(2)(a) of Part III of Schedule 2 to the Income Support Regulations, the sum specified in each case`)'s `the sum after the Order`

@export What is the sum in paragraph 2(1) of Part I of Schedule 2 to the Income Support Regulations after the Order (art 20(3)(b))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the sum in paragraph 2(1) of Part I of Schedule 2 to the Income Support Regulations after the Order` IS
    (`art 20(3)(b): paragraph 2(1) of Part I of Schedule 2 to the Income Support Regulations, sub-paragraphs (a) and (b) of column (2) of the table`)'s `the sum after the Order`

@export What is my family premium in income support after the Order (art 20(4))?
GIVEN `the sub-paragraph of paragraph 3(1)` IS A `a sub-paragraph of paragraph 3(1) of Schedule 2 to the Income Support Regulations` @desc Which sub-paragraph of paragraph 3(1) of Schedule 2 to the Income Support Regulations gives your family premium?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my family premium in income support after the Order` IS
    (`art 20(4): the replaced and the replacing sum` `the sub-paragraph of paragraph 3(1)`)'s `the sum after the Order`

-- art 21: the Order states no rounding, so the exact product is returned (see NOTES.md).
@export What is my special transitional addition to income support after the increase of 3.8 per cent (art 21)?
GIVEN `my special transitional addition before the Order` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your special transitional addition to income support under regulation 15 of the Income Support (Transitional) Regulations 1987 now, before the Order, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my special transitional addition to income support after the increase of 3.8 per cent` IS
    `art 21: the special transitional addition after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `my special transitional addition before the Order`

@export What is the relevant sum for income support in a trade dispute after the Order (art 22)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the relevant sum for income support in a trade dispute after the Order` IS
    (`art 22: section 126(7) of the Contributions and Benefits Act, the relevant sum (trade disputes)`)'s `the sum after the Order`

§§ `Income support: personal allowances (Schedule 2 to the Order)`

@export What is my personal allowance in income support as a single claimant (Sch 2 (1))?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you?
      `I fall within a circumstance specified in paragraph 1A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fall within any of the circumstances specified in paragraph 1A of Schedule 2 to the Income Support Regulations?
      `I satisfy the condition in paragraph 11(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the condition in paragraph 11(1)(a) of Schedule 2 to the Income Support Regulations?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my personal allowance in income support as a single claimant` IS
    `Sch 2 (1): the personal allowance of a single claimant` `my age` `I fall within a circumstance specified in paragraph 1A` `I satisfy the condition in paragraph 11(1)(a)`

@export What is my personal allowance in income support as a lone parent (Sch 2 (2))?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you?
      `I fall within a circumstance specified in paragraph 1A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fall within any of the circumstances specified in paragraph 1A of Schedule 2 to the Income Support Regulations?
      `I satisfy the condition in paragraph 11(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the condition in paragraph 11(1)(a) of Schedule 2 to the Income Support Regulations?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my personal allowance in income support as a lone parent` IS
    `Sch 2 (2): the personal allowance of a lone parent` `my age` `I fall within a circumstance specified in paragraph 1A` `I satisfy the condition in paragraph 11(1)(a)`

-- Schedule 2 (3): a claimant under 18 whose partner is 18 or over, and who is within none of heads (e)(i) to (iii), is
-- reached by no head; the answer is NOTHING.
@export What is our personal allowance in income support as a couple (Sch 2 (3))?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you?
      `my partner's age` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is your partner?
      `at least one of us is treated as responsible for a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is at least one of you treated as responsible for a child?
      `I qualify for income support under regulation 4ZA or income-related ESA, or would if we were not a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you qualify for income support under regulation 4ZA or for income-related employment and support allowance, or would you if you were not a couple?
      `my partner qualifies for income support under regulation 4ZA or income-related ESA, or would if we were not a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your partner qualify for income support under regulation 4ZA or for income-related employment and support allowance, or would they if you were not a couple?
      `I satisfy the requirements of section 3(1)(f)(iii) of the Jobseekers Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the requirements of section 3(1)(f)(iii) of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (prescribed circumstances for persons aged 16 but less than 18)?
      `my partner satisfies the requirements of section 3(1)(f)(iii) of the Jobseekers Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your partner satisfy the requirements of section 3(1)(f)(iii) of the Jobseekers Act 1995?
      `a section 16 direction is in force in respect of me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a direction under section 16 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (severe hardship) in force in respect of you?
      `a section 16 direction is in force in respect of my partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a direction under section 16 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 in force in respect of your partner?
      `one of us falls within a circumstance specified in paragraph 1A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does one of you fall within any of the circumstances specified in paragraph 1A of Schedule 2 to the Income Support Regulations?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is our personal allowance in income support as a couple` IS
    `Sch 2 (3): the personal allowance of a couple` `my age` `my partner's age` `at least one of us is treated as responsible for a child` `I qualify for income support under regulation 4ZA or income-related ESA, or would if we were not a couple` `my partner qualifies for income support under regulation 4ZA or income-related ESA, or would if we were not a couple` `I satisfy the requirements of section 3(1)(f)(iii) of the Jobseekers Act 1995` `my partner satisfies the requirements of section 3(1)(f)(iii) of the Jobseekers Act 1995` `a section 16 direction is in force in respect of me` `a section 16 direction is in force in respect of my partner` `one of us falls within a circumstance specified in paragraph 1A`

§§ `Income support: premiums (Schedule 3 to the Order)`

@export What is my pensioner premium in income support where paragraph 9 applies to me (Sch 3 (2))?
