GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my carer premium in housing benefit (SPC)` IS
    `Sch 7 (4): the carer premium` `the number of persons who satisfy the condition in paragraph 9`

-- The Order states the same fifteen sums for six benefits. Each article names only 'non-dependant deductions'; what each
-- sum is a deduction for is in the parent instrument.
§§ `Non-dependant deductions (articles 20(6), 23(3), 24(3), 26(7), 29(4) and 30(7))`

-- The seat's own choice of benefit: the six articles state the same fifteen sums, one set for each of these benefits.
DECLARE `a benefit whose non-dependant deductions the Order changes` IS ONE OF
    `income support (art 20(6))`
    `housing benefit (art 23(3))`
    `housing benefit for persons over the qualifying age for state pension credit (art 24(3))`
    `jobseeker's allowance under the 1996 Regulations (art 26(7))`
    `state pension credit (art 29(4))`
    `employment and support allowance under the 2008 Regulations (art 30(7))`

@export What is my non-dependant deduction after the Order (arts 20(6), 23(3), 24(3), 26(7), 29(4) and 30(7))?
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A `a benefit whose non-dependant deductions the Order changes` @desc Which benefit is it?
      `the sub-paragraph` IS A `a sub-paragraph of a non-dependant deduction provision` @desc Which sub-paragraph of the non-dependant deductions provision is it?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my non-dependant deduction after the Order` IS
    CONSIDER `the benefit`
    WHEN `income support (art 20(6))` THEN (`art 20(6): the replaced and the replacing sum in the non-dependant deductions` `the sub-paragraph`)'s `the sum after the Order`
    WHEN `housing benefit (art 23(3))` THEN (`art 23(3): the replaced and the replacing sum in the non-dependant deductions` `the sub-paragraph`)'s `the sum after the Order`
    WHEN `housing benefit for persons over the qualifying age for state pension credit (art 24(3))` THEN (`art 24(3): the replaced and the replacing sum in the non-dependant deductions` `the sub-paragraph`)'s `the sum after the Order`
    WHEN `jobseeker's allowance under the 1996 Regulations (art 26(7))` THEN (`art 26(7): the replaced and the replacing sum in the non-dependant deductions` `the sub-paragraph`)'s `the sum after the Order`
    WHEN `state pension credit (art 29(4))` THEN (`art 29(4): the replaced and the replacing sum in the non-dependant deductions` `the sub-paragraph`)'s `the sum after the Order`
    WHEN `employment and support allowance under the 2008 Regulations (art 30(7))` THEN (`art 30(7): the replaced and the replacing sum in the non-dependant deductions` `the sub-paragraph`)'s `the sum after the Order`

§ `Part 4: jobseeker's allowance (articles 25 to 28 and Schedules 8 to 10)`

@export What is my weekly amount of contribution-based jobseeker's allowance after the Order (art 25)?
GIVEN `the sub-paragraph of regulation 79(1)` IS A `a sub-paragraph of regulation 79(1) of the JSA Regulations 1996` @desc Which sub-paragraph of regulation 79(1) of the Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 1996 gives your amount?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my weekly amount of contribution-based jobseeker's allowance after the Order` IS
    (`art 25: the replaced and the replacing sum` `the sub-paragraph of regulation 79(1)`)'s `the sum after the Order`

-- art 26(2): the sum specified in each of five places is 3,000 and remains unchanged.
@export What is the sum of 3,000 in the jobseeker's allowance rules after the Order (art 26(2))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the sum of 3,000 in the jobseeker's allowance rules after the Order` IS
    (`art 26(2): regulations 83(b), 84(1)(c) and 85(1) and paragraphs 15A(2)(a) and 16(2)(a) of Part III of Schedule 1 to the JSA Regulations 1996, the sum specified in each case`)'s `the sum after the Order`

@export What is the sum in paragraph 2(1) of Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the JSA Regulations 1996 after the Order (art 26(3)(b))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the sum in paragraph 2(1) of Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the JSA Regulations 1996 after the Order` IS
    (`art 26(3)(b): paragraph 2(1) of Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the JSA Regulations 1996, sub-paragraphs (a) and (b) of column (2) of the table`)'s `the sum after the Order`

@export What is my family premium in jobseeker's allowance after the Order (art 26(4))?
GIVEN `the sub-paragraph of paragraph 4(1)` IS A `a sub-paragraph of paragraph 4(1) of Part II of Schedule 1 to the JSA Regulations 1996` @desc Which sub-paragraph of paragraph 4(1) of Part II of Schedule 1 to the Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 1996 gives your family premium?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my family premium in jobseeker's allowance after the Order` IS
    (`art 26(4): the replaced and the replacing sum` `the sub-paragraph of paragraph 4(1)`)'s `the sum after the Order`

@export What is the prescribed sum for a trade dispute in jobseeker's allowance after the Order (art 27)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the prescribed sum for a trade dispute in jobseeker's allowance after the Order` IS
    (`art 27: regulation 172 of the JSA Regulations 1996, the prescribed sum (trade disputes)`)'s `the sum after the Order`

@export What is my weekly amount of jobseeker's allowance under the 2013 Regulations after the Order (art 28)?
GIVEN `the sub-paragraph of regulation 49(1)` IS A `a sub-paragraph of regulation 49(1) of the JSA Regulations 2013` @desc Which sub-paragraph of regulation 49(1) of the Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 2013 gives your amount?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my weekly amount of jobseeker's allowance under the 2013 Regulations after the Order` IS
    (`art 28: the replaced and the replacing sum` `the sub-paragraph of regulation 49(1)`)'s `the sum after the Order`

§§ `Jobseeker's allowance: personal allowances (Schedule 8 to the Order)`

@export What is my personal allowance in jobseeker's allowance as a single claimant (Sch 8 (1))?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you?
      `I fall within paragraph (2) of regulation 57` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fall within paragraph (2) of regulation 57 of the Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 1996?
      `regulation 59, 60 or 61 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 59, 60 or 61 of the Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 1996 apply to you?
      `a section 16 direction is in force in respect of me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a direction under section 16 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (severe hardship) in force in respect of you?
      `I satisfy the condition in paragraph 13(1)(a) of Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the condition in paragraph 13(1)(a) of Part 3?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my personal allowance in jobseeker's allowance as a single claimant` IS
    `Sch 8 (1): the personal allowance of a single claimant` `my age` `I fall within paragraph (2) of regulation 57` `regulation 59, 60 or 61 applies to me` `a section 16 direction is in force in respect of me` `I satisfy the condition in paragraph 13(1)(a) of Part 3`

@export What is my personal allowance in jobseeker's allowance as a lone parent (Sch 8 (2))?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you?
      `I fall within paragraph (2) of regulation 57` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fall within paragraph (2) of regulation 57 of the Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 1996?
      `regulation 59, 60 or 61 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 59, 60 or 61 of the Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 1996 apply to you?
      `a section 16 direction is in force in respect of me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a direction under section 16 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (severe hardship) in force in respect of you?
      `I satisfy the condition in paragraph 13(1)(a) of Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the condition in paragraph 13(1)(a) of Part 3?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my personal allowance in jobseeker's allowance as a lone parent` IS
    `Sch 8 (2): the personal allowance of a lone parent` `my age` `I fall within paragraph (2) of regulation 57` `regulation 59, 60 or 61 applies to me` `a section 16 direction is in force in respect of me` `I satisfy the condition in paragraph 13(1)(a) of Part 3`

-- Schedule 8 (3): each head is tried in the order the Schedule prints it. Both members under 18 and within none of heads
-- (a) to (d) is NOTHING.
@export What is our personal allowance in jobseeker's allowance as a couple (Sch 8 (3))?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you?
      `regulation 59, 60 or 61 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 59, 60 or 61 of the Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 1996 apply to you?
      `regulation 59, 60 or 61 would apply to me if we were not a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would regulation 59, 60 or 61 apply to you if you were not a member of a couple?
      `I am registered in accordance with regulation 62` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you registered in accordance with regulation 62?
      `I fall within paragraph (2) of regulation 57` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fall within paragraph (2) of regulation 57?
      `a section 16 direction is in force in respect of me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a direction under section 16 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 in force in respect of you?
      `I satisfy the requirements for income support, other than making a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the requirements for entitlement to income support, other than the requirement to make a claim?
      `I would satisfy the requirements for income support, other than making a claim, if we were not a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you satisfy the requirements for entitlement to income support, other than the requirement to make a claim, if you were not a member of a couple?
      `I satisfy the requirements for income-related employment and support allowance, other than making a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the requirements for entitlement to an income-related employment and support allowance, other than the requirement to make a claim?
      `I satisfy the requirements of paragraph 13(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the requirements of paragraph 13(1)(a)?
      `I am treated as responsible for a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you treated as responsible for a child?
      `my partner's age` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is your partner?
      `regulation 59, 60 or 61 applies to my partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 59, 60 or 61 of the Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 1996 apply to your partner?
      `regulation 59, 60 or 61 would apply to my partner if we were not a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would regulation 59, 60 or 61 apply to your partner if you were not a couple?
      `my partner is registered in accordance with regulation 62` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner registered in accordance with regulation 62?
      `my partner falls within paragraph (2) of regulation 57` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your partner fall within paragraph (2) of regulation 57?
      `a section 16 direction is in force in respect of my partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a direction under section 16 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 in force in respect of your partner?
      `my partner satisfies the requirements for income support, other than making a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your partner satisfy the requirements for entitlement to income support, other than the requirement to make a claim?
      `my partner would satisfy the requirements for income support, other than making a claim, if we were not a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your partner satisfy the requirements for entitlement to income support, other than the requirement to make a claim, if you were not a couple?
      `my partner satisfies the requirements for income-related employment and support allowance, other than making a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your partner satisfy the requirements for entitlement to an income-related employment and support allowance, other than the requirement to make a claim?
      `my partner satisfies the requirements of paragraph 13(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your partner satisfy the requirements of paragraph 13(1)(a)?
      `my partner is treated as responsible for a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner treated as responsible for a child?
      `we are married or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and your partner married or civil partners?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is our personal allowance in jobseeker's allowance as a couple` IS
    `Sch 8 (3): the personal allowance of a couple` `me` `my partner` `we are married or civil partners`
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS `a member of a couple claiming jobseeker's allowance` WITH
            `the member's age` IS `my age`
            `regulation 59, 60 or 61 applies to the member` IS `regulation 59, 60 or 61 applies to me`
            `regulation 59, 60 or 61 would apply to the member if they were not a member of a couple` IS `regulation 59, 60 or 61 would apply to me if we were not a couple`
            `the member is registered in accordance with regulation 62` IS `I am registered in accordance with regulation 62`
            `the member falls within paragraph (2) of regulation 57` IS `I fall within paragraph (2) of regulation 57`
            `a direction under section 16 is in force in respect of the member` IS `a section 16 direction is in force in respect of me`
            `the member satisfies the requirements for entitlement to income support, other than the requirement to make a claim` IS `I satisfy the requirements for income support, other than making a claim`
            `the member would satisfy the requirements for entitlement to income support, other than the requirement to make a claim, if they were not a member of a couple` IS `I would satisfy the requirements for income support, other than making a claim, if we were not a couple`
            `the member satisfies the requirements for entitlement to an income-related employment and support allowance, other than the requirement to make a claim` IS `I satisfy the requirements for income-related employment and support allowance, other than making a claim`
            `the member satisfies the requirements of paragraph 13(1)(a)` IS `I satisfy the requirements of paragraph 13(1)(a)`
            `the member is treated as responsible for a child` IS `I am treated as responsible for a child`
        `my partner` MEANS `a member of a couple claiming jobseeker's allowance` WITH
            `the member's age` IS `my partner's age`
            `regulation 59, 60 or 61 applies to the member` IS `regulation 59, 60 or 61 applies to my partner`
            `regulation 59, 60 or 61 would apply to the member if they were not a member of a couple` IS `regulation 59, 60 or 61 would apply to my partner if we were not a couple`
            `the member is registered in accordance with regulation 62` IS `my partner is registered in accordance with regulation 62`
            `the member falls within paragraph (2) of regulation 57` IS `my partner falls within paragraph (2) of regulation 57`
            `a direction under section 16 is in force in respect of the member` IS `a section 16 direction is in force in respect of my partner`
            `the member satisfies the requirements for entitlement to income support, other than the requirement to make a claim` IS `my partner satisfies the requirements for income support, other than making a claim`
            `the member would satisfy the requirements for entitlement to income support, other than the requirement to make a claim, if they were not a member of a couple` IS `my partner would satisfy the requirements for income support, other than making a claim, if we were not a couple`
            `the member satisfies the requirements for entitlement to an income-related employment and support allowance, other than the requirement to make a claim` IS `my partner satisfies the requirements for income-related employment and support allowance, other than making a claim`
            `the member satisfies the requirements of paragraph 13(1)(a)` IS `my partner satisfies the requirements of paragraph 13(1)(a)`
            `the member is treated as responsible for a child` IS `my partner is treated as responsible for a child`

§§ `Jobseeker's allowance: premiums (Schedules 9 and 10 to the Order)`

@export What is my pensioner premium in jobseeker's allowance (qualifying age for state pension credit) (Sch 9 (2))?
GIVEN `the condition I satisfy` IS A `a condition of paragraph 10 of Part III of Schedule 1 to the JSA Regulations 1996` @desc Which condition of paragraph 10 of Part III of Schedule 1 to the Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 1996 do you satisfy?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my pensioner premium in jobseeker's allowance (qualifying age for state pension credit)` IS
    `Sch 9 (2): the pensioner premium for persons who have attained the qualifying age for state pension credit` `the condition I satisfy`

@export What is my pensioner premium in jobseeker's allowance where my partner is 75 or over (Sch 9 (3))?
GIVEN `I satisfy the condition in paragraph 11` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the condition in paragraph 11 (your partner has attained the age of 75)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my pensioner premium in jobseeker's allowance where my partner is 75 or over` IS
    `Sch 9 (3): the pensioner premium for claimants whose partner has attained the age of 75` `I satisfy the condition in paragraph 11`

@export What is my higher pensioner premium in jobseeker's allowance (Sch 9 (4))?
GIVEN `the condition I satisfy` IS A `a condition of paragraph 12(1) of Part III of Schedule 1 to the JSA Regulations 1996` @desc Which condition of paragraph 12(1) of Part III of Schedule 1 to the Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 1996 do you satisfy?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my higher pensioner premium in jobseeker's allowance` IS
    `Sch 9 (4): the higher pensioner premium` `the condition I satisfy`

@export What is my disability premium in jobseeker's allowance (Sch 9 (5))?
GIVEN `the condition I satisfy` IS A `a condition of paragraph 13(1) of Part III of Schedule 1 to the JSA Regulations 1996` @desc Which condition of paragraph 13(1) of Part III of Schedule 1 to the Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 1996 do you satisfy?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my disability premium in jobseeker's allowance` IS
    `Sch 9 (5): the disability premium` `the condition I satisfy`

@export What is my severe disability premium in jobseeker's allowance (Sch 9 (6))?
GIVEN `the condition I satisfy` IS A `a condition of paragraph 15 of Part III of Schedule 1 to the JSA Regulations 1996` @desc Which condition of paragraph 15 of Part III of Schedule 1 to the Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 1996 do you satisfy?
      `someone is in receipt of a carer's allowance or carer support payment for me, or a partner satisfies the condition by virtue of paragraph 15(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is someone in receipt of a carer's allowance or carer support payment for you, or does a partner of yours satisfy the condition by virtue of paragraph 15(5)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my severe disability premium in jobseeker's allowance` IS
    `Sch 9 (6): the severe disability premium` `the condition I satisfy` `someone is in receipt of a carer's allowance or carer support payment for me, or a partner satisfies the condition by virtue of paragraph 15(5)`

@export What is my disabled child premium in jobseeker's allowance (Sch 9 (7))?
GIVEN `the number of children and young persons for whom the conditions in paragraph 16 are satisfied` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many children and young persons are the conditions in paragraph 16 satisfied?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my disabled child premium in jobseeker's allowance` IS
    `Sch 9 (7): the disabled child premium` `the number of children and young persons for whom the conditions in paragraph 16 are satisfied`

@export What is my carer premium in jobseeker's allowance (Sch 9 (8))?
GIVEN `the number of persons who satisfy the condition in paragraph 17` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons satisfy the condition in paragraph 17?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my carer premium in jobseeker's allowance` IS
    `Sch 9 (8): the carer premium` `the number of persons who satisfy the condition in paragraph 17`

@export What is my enhanced disability premium in jobseeker's allowance for children and young persons (Sch 9 (9)(a))?
GIVEN `the number of children and young persons for whom the conditions in paragraph 15A are satisfied` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many children and young persons are the conditions in paragraph 15A satisfied?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my enhanced disability premium in jobseeker's allowance for children and young persons` IS
    `Sch 9 (9)(a): the enhanced disability premium for children and young persons` `the number of children and young persons for whom the conditions in paragraph 15A are satisfied`

@export What is my enhanced disability premium in jobseeker's allowance if I am neither a child or young person nor in a couple (Sch 9 (9)(b))?
GIVEN `I am neither a child or young person nor a member of a couple or polygamous marriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you neither a child or young person nor a member of a couple or a polygamous marriage?
      `the conditions in paragraph 15A are satisfied in respect of me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the conditions in paragraph 15A satisfied in respect of you?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my enhanced disability premium in jobseeker's allowance if I am neither a child or young person nor in a couple` IS
    `Sch 9 (9)(b): the enhanced disability premium for a person who is neither a child or young person nor in a couple` `I am neither a child or young person nor a member of a couple or polygamous marriage` `the conditions in paragraph 15A are satisfied in respect of me`

@export What is my enhanced disability premium in jobseeker's allowance if I am in a couple (Sch 9 (9)(c))?
GIVEN `I am a member of a couple or polygamous marriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of a couple or a polygamous marriage?
      `the conditions in paragraph 15A are satisfied in respect of a member of our couple or polygamous marriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the conditions in paragraph 15A satisfied in respect of a member of your couple or polygamous marriage?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my enhanced disability premium in jobseeker's allowance if I am in a couple` IS
    `Sch 9 (9)(c): the enhanced disability premium for a member of a couple or polygamous marriage` `I am a member of a couple or polygamous marriage` `the conditions in paragraph 15A are satisfied in respect of a member of our couple or polygamous marriage`

@export What is our pensioner premium in jobseeker's allowance as a joint-claim couple (Sch 10 (1))?
GIVEN `one of us has attained the qualifying age for state pension credit and the condition in paragraph 20E is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has one of you attained the qualifying age for state pension credit, and is the condition in paragraph 20E satisfied?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is our pensioner premium in jobseeker's allowance as a joint-claim couple` IS
    `Sch 10 (1): the pensioner premium for a joint-claim couple` `one of us has attained the qualifying age for state pension credit and the condition in paragraph 20E is satisfied`

@export What is our higher pensioner premium in jobseeker's allowance as a joint-claim couple (Sch 10 (2))?
GIVEN `one of us satisfies the condition in paragraph 20F` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does one of you satisfy the condition in paragraph 20F?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is our higher pensioner premium in jobseeker's allowance as a joint-claim couple` IS
    `Sch 10 (2): the higher pensioner premium for a joint-claim couple` `one of us satisfies the condition in paragraph 20F`

@export What is our disability premium in jobseeker's allowance as a joint-claim couple (Sch 10 (3))?
GIVEN `one of us satisfies the condition in paragraph 20G(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does one of you satisfy the condition in paragraph 20G(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is our disability premium in jobseeker's allowance as a joint-claim couple` IS
    `Sch 10 (3): the disability premium for a joint-claim couple` `one of us satisfies the condition in paragraph 20G(1)`

@export What is our severe disability premium in jobseeker's allowance as a joint-claim couple (Sch 10 (4))?
GIVEN `one of us satisfies the condition in paragraph 20I(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does one of you satisfy the condition in paragraph 20I(1)?
      `someone is in receipt of a carer's allowance or carer support payment for us, or either of us satisfies the condition only by virtue of paragraph 20I(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is someone in receipt of a carer's allowance or carer support payment for you, or does either of you satisfy the condition only by virtue of paragraph 20I(4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is our severe disability premium in jobseeker's allowance as a joint-claim couple` IS
    `Sch 10 (4): the severe disability premium for a joint-claim couple` `one of us satisfies the condition in paragraph 20I(1)` `someone is in receipt of a carer's allowance or carer support payment for us, or either of us satisfies the condition only by virtue of paragraph 20I(4)`

@export What is our carer premium in jobseeker's allowance as a joint-claim couple (Sch 10 (5))?
GIVEN `the number of persons who satisfy the condition in paragraph 20J` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons satisfy the condition in paragraph 20J?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is our carer premium in jobseeker's allowance as a joint-claim couple` IS
    `Sch 10 (5): the carer premium for a joint-claim couple` `the number of persons who satisfy the condition in paragraph 20J`

@export What is our enhanced disability premium in jobseeker's allowance as a joint-claim couple (Sch 10 (6))?
GIVEN `the conditions in paragraph 20IA are satisfied in respect of one of us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the conditions in paragraph 20IA satisfied in respect of one of you?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is our enhanced disability premium in jobseeker's allowance as a joint-claim couple` IS
    `Sch 10 (6): the enhanced disability premium for a joint-claim couple` `the conditions in paragraph 20IA are satisfied in respect of one of us`

§ `Part 5: state pension credit (article 29)`

@export What is my guarantee credit sum in state pension credit after the Order (art 29(2))?
GIVEN `the provision of regulation 6` IS A `a sum in regulation 6 of the State Pension Credit Regulations` @desc Which provision of regulation 6 of the State Pension Credit Regulations 2002 gives your sum?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my guarantee credit sum in state pension credit after the Order` IS
    (`art 29(2): the replaced and the replacing sum` `the provision of regulation 6`)'s `the sum after the Order`

@export What is my savings credit sum in state pension credit after the Order (art 29(3))?
GIVEN `the sum in regulation 7(2)` IS A `a sum in regulation 7(2) of the State Pension Credit Regulations` @desc Which of the two sums in regulation 7(2) of the State Pension Credit Regulations 2002 is it?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my savings credit sum in state pension credit after the Order` IS
    (`art 29(3): the replaced and the replacing sum` `the sum in regulation 7(2)`)'s `the sum after the Order`

@export What is my additional amount for a child in state pension credit after the Order (art 29(5) and (6))?
GIVEN `the sum in Schedule IIA` IS A `a sum in Schedule IIA to the State Pension Credit Regulations` @desc Which sum in Schedule IIA to the State Pension Credit Regulations 2002 is it?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my additional amount for a child in state pension credit after the Order` IS
    (`art 29(5) and (6): the replaced and the replacing sum` `the sum in Schedule IIA`)'s `the sum after the Order`

@export What is my sum in state pension credit for a polygamous marriage after the Order (art 29(7))?
GIVEN `the sum in paragraph 1 of Schedule III` IS A `a sum in paragraph 1 of Schedule III to the State Pension Credit Regulations` @desc Which sum in paragraph 1 of Schedule III to the State Pension Credit Regulations 2002 is it?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my sum in state pension credit for a polygamous marriage after the Order` IS
    (`art 29(7): the replaced and the replacing sum` `the sum in paragraph 1 of Schedule III`)'s `the sum after the Order`

§ `Part 6: employment and support allowance (articles 30 and 31 and Schedules 11 and 12)`

-- Schedule 11 prints only the rows for a single claimant (paragraph 1 for the usual case, paragraph 2 for cases within
-- paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the 2017 Regulations).
@export What is my prescribed amount in employment and support allowance as a single claimant (art 30(2) and (3))?
GIVEN `my case falls within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the ESA and UC Regulations 2017` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your case fall within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the Employment and Support Allowance and Universal Credit (Miscellaneous Amendments and Transitional and Savings Provisions) Regulations 2017?
      `I satisfy the conditions set out in section 2(2) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the conditions set out in section 2(2) of the Act?
      `I satisfy the conditions set out in section 2(3) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the conditions set out in section 2(3) of the Act?
      `I am a member of the work-related activity group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the work-related activity group?
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my prescribed amount in employment and support allowance as a single claimant` IS
    `art 30(2) and (3): the prescribed amount for a single claimant` `my case falls within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the ESA and UC Regulations 2017` `I satisfy the conditions set out in section 2(2) of the Act` `I satisfy the conditions set out in section 2(3) of the Act` `I am a member of the work-related activity group` `my age`

-- The text prints two tables whose paragraph markers were lost; the first (with the carer premium, without the
-- work-related activity rows) is taken as paragraph 1 and the second as paragraph 2 (see NOTES.md).
@export What is my pensioner premium in employment and support allowance (art 30(4) and (5))?
GIVEN `my case falls within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the ESA and UC Regulations 2017` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your case fall within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the Employment and Support Allowance and Universal Credit (Miscellaneous Amendments and Transitional and Savings Provisions) Regulations 2017?
      `paragraph 5 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does paragraph 5 of Schedule 4 to the Employment and Support Allowance Regulations 2008 apply to you?
      `I am a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of a couple?
      `I am entitled to the support component` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to the support component?
      `I am entitled to the work-related activity component` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to the work-related activity component?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my pensioner premium in employment and support allowance` IS
    `art 30(4) and (5): the pensioner premium` `my case falls within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the ESA and UC Regulations 2017` `paragraph 5 applies to me` `I am a member of a couple` `I am entitled to the support component` `I am entitled to the work-related activity component`

-- In a case within paragraphs 2 to 7 the Order sets only paragraph 11(1) (art 30(5)); it sets no sum for the carer
-- premium in paragraph 11(3).
@export What is my carer premium in employment and support allowance (art 30(4) and (5))?
GIVEN `my case falls within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the ESA and UC Regulations 2017` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your case fall within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the Employment and Support Allowance and Universal Credit (Miscellaneous Amendments and Transitional and Savings Provisions) Regulations 2017?
      `the number of persons who satisfy the condition specified in paragraph 8(1)` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons satisfy the condition specified in paragraph 8(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my carer premium in employment and support allowance` IS
    `art 30(4) and (5): the carer premium` `my case falls within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the ESA and UC Regulations 2017` `the number of persons who satisfy the condition specified in paragraph 8(1)`

@export What is my work-related activity component for a contributory allowance after the Order (art 30(6)(b))?
GIVEN `my case falls within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the ESA and UC Regulations 2017` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your case fall within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the Employment and Support Allowance and Universal Credit (Miscellaneous Amendments and Transitional and Savings Provisions) Regulations 2017?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my work-related activity component for a contributory allowance after the Order` IS
    `art 30(6)(b): the amount of the work-related activity component for the purposes of a contributory allowance` `my case falls within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the ESA and UC Regulations 2017`

@export What is my support component for a contributory allowance after the Order (art 30(6)(c))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my support component for a contributory allowance after the Order` IS
    `art 30(6)(c): the amount of the support component for the purposes of a contributory allowance`

@export What is my prescribed amount in employment and support allowance under the 2013 Regulations after the Order (art 31(1))?
GIVEN `the provision of regulation 62` IS A `a sub-paragraph of regulation 62 of the ESA Regulations 2013` @desc Which provision of regulation 62 of the Employment and Support Allowance Regulations 2013 gives your amount?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my prescribed amount in employment and support allowance under the 2013 Regulations after the Order` IS
    (`art 31(1): the replaced and the replacing sum` `the provision of regulation 62`)'s `the sum after the Order`

@export What is my regulation 62(2) amount after the Order in a case within paragraphs 2 to 7 (art 31(2))?
GIVEN `the sub-paragraph of regulation 62(2)` IS A `a sub-paragraph of regulation 62(2) of the ESA Regulations 2013` @desc Which sub-paragraph of regulation 62(2) of the Employment and Support Allowance Regulations 2013 gives your amount?
      `my case falls within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the ESA and UC Regulations 2017` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your case fall within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the Employment and Support Allowance and Universal Credit (Miscellaneous Amendments and Transitional and Savings Provisions) Regulations 2017?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my regulation 62(2) amount after the Order in a case within paragraphs 2 to 7` IS
    CONSIDER `art 31(2): the sums in a case falling within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the ESA and UC Regulations 2017` `the sub-paragraph of regulation 62(2)` `my case falls within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the ESA and UC Regulations 2017`
    WHEN JUST `the pair` THEN JUST (`the pair`'s `the sum after the Order`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@export What is my modified regulation 62 amount after the Order (art 31(3))?
GIVEN `the sub-paragraph of regulation 62(1)(a)` IS A `a sub-paragraph of regulation 62(1)(a) of the ESA Regulations 2013 as modified` @desc Which sub-paragraph of regulation 62(1)(a) of the Employment and Support Allowance Regulations 2013, as modified, gives your amount?
      `regulation 62 applies to me as modified by the 2010 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 62 apply to you as modified by paragraph 12 of Schedule 2 to the Employment and Support Allowance (Transitional Provisions, Housing Benefit and Council Tax Benefit) (Existing Awards) (No. 2) Regulations 2010, as that paragraph is modified by paragraph 21(10) of Schedule 4 to the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (Commencement No. 9 and Transitional and Transitory Provisions and Commencement No. 8 and Savings and Transitional Provisions (Amendment)) Order 2013?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my modified regulation 62 amount after the Order` IS
    CONSIDER `art 31(3): the sums in regulation 62 as modified` `the sub-paragraph of regulation 62(1)(a)` `regulation 62 applies to me as modified by the 2010 Regulations`
    WHEN JUST `the pair` THEN JUST (`the pair`'s `the sum after the Order`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§ `Part 7: universal credit (articles 32 and 33 and Schedule 13)`

@export What is my work allowance sum in universal credit after the Order (art 32(1))?
GIVEN `the sum in the table in regulation 22` IS A `a sum in the table in regulation 22 of the Universal Credit Regulations` @desc Which sum in the table in regulation 22 of the Universal Credit Regulations 2013 is it?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my work allowance sum in universal credit after the Order` IS
    (`art 32(1): the replaced and the replacing sum` `the sum in the table in regulation 22`)'s `the sum after the Order`

@export What is my housing cost contribution in universal credit after the Order (art 32(3))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my housing cost contribution in universal credit after the Order` IS
    (`art 32(3): paragraph 14(1) of Schedule 4 to the Universal Credit Regulations, the amount of housing cost contributions`)'s `the sum after the Order`

@export What is my sum in the severe disability premium protection in universal credit after the Order (art 33(a))?
GIVEN `the sum in paragraph 5 of Schedule 2` IS A `a sum in paragraph 5 of Schedule 2 to the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014` @desc Which sum in paragraph 5 of Schedule 2 to the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014 is it?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my sum in the severe disability premium protection in universal credit after the Order` IS
    (`art 33(a): the replaced and the replacing sum` `the sum in paragraph 5 of Schedule 2`)'s `the sum after the Order`

@export What is my additional amount in the transitional protection in universal credit after the Order (art 33(b))?
GIVEN `the sum in paragraph 5 of Schedule 3` IS A `a sum in paragraph 5 of Schedule 3 to the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014` @desc Which sum in paragraph 5 of Schedule 3 to the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014 is it?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my additional amount in the transitional protection in universal credit after the Order` IS
    (`art 33(b): the replaced and the replacing sum` `the sum in paragraph 5 of Schedule 3`)'s `the sum after the Order`

@export What is the child element in universal credit for my child (Sch 13)?
GIVEN `the place of my child in the order of my children` IS A NUMBER @desc Is the child your first child or qualifying young person (give 1), or your second or a later one (give 2, 3 and so on)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the child element in universal credit for my child` IS
    `Sch 13: the child element for the child or qualifying young person` `the place of my child in the order of my children`

@export What is the additional amount in universal credit for my disabled child (Sch 13)?
GIVEN `the rate` IS A `a rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` @desc Is the child entitled to the lower rate or the higher rate of the additional amount?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the additional amount in universal credit for my disabled child` IS
    `Sch 13: the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` `the rate`

@export What is the carer element in universal credit (Sch 13)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the carer element in universal credit` IS
    `Sch 13: the carer element`

@export What is the most I can get for childcare costs in universal credit (Sch 13)?
GIVEN `the number of my children` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many children are you claiming childcare costs?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can get for childcare costs in universal credit` IS
    `Sch 13: the maximum amount of the childcare costs element` `the number of my children`

§ `Part 8: revocation (article 34)`

-- art 34 comes into force on 5 May 2026 (art 1(3)(o)). The Order says nothing about savings or rights that accrued under
-- the revoked Order.
@export Has the Social Security Benefits Up-rating Order 2025 been revoked on this date (art 34)?
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you ask?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the Social Security Benefits Up-rating Order 2025 been revoked on this date` IF
    `art 34: the Social Security Benefits Up-rating Order 2025 has been revoked on the date` `the date`
